// An array Sysl may write is written back only as a binding's own parameter, of bytes, integers,
// reals, booleans or characters. Anywhere else, an array crosses as a copy Sysl may only read, so a
// Sysl type that would let it write is refused rather than given a copy whose writes are lost: an
// array of strings, an array an option holds, and an array a mirror's field holds.
// error: the Sysl binding `names` does not match `avintest.digits.name_all`: Sysl may write the elements of its `[]string`, and an `Array` there crosses as a copy it may only read, so what it wrote would never reach the array: an `Array` is written back only as the binding's own parameter, of bytes, integers, reals, booleans or characters
// error: the Sysl binding `maybeFill` does not match `avintest.digits.fill_maybe`: Sysl may write the elements of its `Option[[]u8]`, and an `Array` there crosses as a copy it may only read, so what it wrote would never reach the array: an `Array` is written back only as the binding's own parameter, of bytes, integers, reals, booleans or characters
// error: the Sysl mirror `Window` does not match `avintest.digits.Window`: Sysl may write the elements of its `[]byte`, and an `Array` there crosses as a copy it may only read, so what it wrote would never reach the array: an `Array` is written back only as the binding's own parameter, of bytes, integers, reals, booleans or characters

@sysl("avintest.digits.name_all")
names(into: Array[string]) -> long

@sysl("avintest.digits.fill_maybe")
maybeFill(n: long, into: Option[Array[byte]]) -> long

@sysl("avintest.digits.Window")
data Window(bytes: Array[byte])

@sysl("avintest.digits.fill_window")
fillWindow(n: long, w: Window) -> long

main()
  println(names(Array.fill(1, "")))
  println(maybeFill(1, Some(Array.fill(1, byte(0)))))
  println(fillWindow(1, Window(Array.fill(1, byte(0)))))
